    "body": "## Summary\n\nCloses ADR-039 as **partial delivery with three honest corrections** in the record. Commit 1 delivered and verified; Commit 2 reverted. **Documentation only — no code changes.**\n\n## What landed and what didn't\n\n| Commit | Feature | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| Commit 1 (#199) | `height` + `min/max` + `overflow: hidden` | ✅ Delivered, verified |\n| Commit 2 (#200) | `box-sizing: border-box` | ❌ Reverted by #201 (visual regression) |\n\n**ADR-037's height gap is closed**: search icon `w=20 h=0` → `w=20 h=20`, verified via tree walk and PNG.\n\n## Three honest corrections preserved\n\n### Correction 1: \"185px gap\" was a misdiagnosis\n\nCommit 1's message claimed article title moved from y=145 to y=330 with a 185px gap introduced. That measurement was taken from the **broken pre-fix render** (percentage height collapse, layout height 1774px). The fixed render was never opened before writing the message.\n\n**Actual measured state**: title at y=128 (baseline was y=145 — 17px *higher*, not 185px lower). No gap. The implementation is slightly better than baseline.\n\nPer ADR-028 pattern: the original claim stays in commit history; this correction preserves both versions.\n\n### Correction 2: `box-sizing` regression + process failure\n\nCommit 2 shipped, merged, then showed **gray strip on left (x≈0-110) + search icon shifted x=386→438** when the merged render was opened. Root cause unmeasured (deferred to re-attempt).\n\n**Process failure**: Commit 2 merged without rendering and visually inspecting the PNG first. Every commit since ADR-034 was visually verified or docs-only; Commit 2 broke the pattern.\n\n**Two-commit split worked as designed**: revert of #200 alone restored Commit 1's verified state. That's the isolation strategy's payoff.\n\n### Correction 3: `border` shorthand limitation surfaced\n\nCommit 2's initial tests used `border: 5px solid black` which ADR-012 doesn't expand (only `border-width` longhand is expanded). Tests were corrected to use `border-width: 5px`; the box-sizing implementation itself was correct.\n\n**Real-world impact**: Wikipedia uses `border: 1px solid X` shorthand in many places — those borders are **currently invisible**. Pre-existing limitation, not introduced by ADR-039. Deferred to a small future ADR (\"border shorthand expansion\", ~20 lines).\n\n## The discipline exercised\n\n**Two patterns preserved**:\n\n1. **Two-commit risk isolation** — worked as designed. Commit 2's regression didn't contaminate Commit 1.\n2. **Revert-with-record** — reverting Commit 2 preserved the original commit in git history, added an honest revert commit, and left the verified Commit 1 state on main. Same principle as ADR-028's correction-in-place, applied to a merged regression.\n\n**New process lesson**: **visual verification is not optional between commit and merge**. The two-stage measurement (ADR-029 onward) applies to risk-isolated commits just as it does to full ADRs — Commit 2's verification step was skipped.\n\n## What's deferred (updated from spec)\n\nOriginal deferred list unchanged, plus two new items:\n\n- `box-sizing: border-box` — re-attempt with proper PNG-before-merge discipline\n- `parent_content_height` threading (unblocks percentage heights)\n- `overflow: auto | scroll`\n- `overflow-wrap`, `aspect-ratio`\n- **NEW**: `border` shorthand expansion\n- **NEW**: box-sizing root cause diagnostic\n\n## Test count\n\n- Before ADR-039: 480 / 1851\n- After Commit 1: **494 / 1881** (+14 / +30)\n- After Commit 2: 500 / 1894\n- After Revert: **494 / 1881** (returned to Commit 1 state)\n- Full suite all pass, zero warnings\n- CI green on #199, #200, #201\n\n## Verification\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Search icon 20×20 | ✅ (kept — Commit 1 delivered) |\n| Layout height 62283 | ✅ |\n| Article title y=128 | ✅ (better than baseline) |\n| No gray strip | ✅ (Commit 2 reverted) |\n| 494 box-model-related tests pass | ✅ |\n| Three corrections in ADR-039 record | ✅ |\n\n## What's next\n\n1. **Pause or re-attempt**: decide whether to pursue box-sizing re-attempt now (with proper verification) or defer to ADR-040+\n2. **ADR-040**: `parent_content_height` + `overflow: auto/scroll` + `border` shorthand expansion + box-sizing re-attempt\n3. **Alternatives**: `:has()`/`:dir()` (ADR-038's deferrals), pseudo-elements, `@font-face`\n\nRefs #198 #199 #200 #201\n",
